    "issue": "63bad95d",
    "purpose": "consumer-family",
    "description": "Confirmation of issue 63bad95d, protocol version 4: every cell is confirmatory and its declaration is the pilot's. Question: is the native build of the profile no worse than its portable build on one primary workload per entry-point group? The baseline arm is the tuned-portable build: default target, simd and tuning-profile features, --cfg gf2_tuning_baked, the measured core owner the plan pins installed before the first selector read. The candidate arm is the native build: the same sources, features, cfg and installed owner with -C target-cpu=native added. The two arms are separate executables of one harness crate and differ in that one flag. Kernel-isolated cells time the public kernel entry on prepared operands; whole-consumer cells time the public BitMatrix call including its output allocation and release. Every cell is warm, single-core and calibrated. The measurement resolution is the widest relative bootstrap half-width of the whole pinned pilot at this confirmation's corrected alpha. The family selects nothing: it reports whether a consumer who builds for the host loses anything against the portable profile build."
  },
